# AEM Console — repo tracks ONLY the Next.js app. /opt/aem-console on the bastion doubles as root's
# working dir and is full of one-off ops scripts, caches and generated files; we deliberately leave all
# of that untracked. Whitelist approach: ignore everything at the root, then re-include the app.

# Ignore everything at the repo root by default…
/*

# …then track the app and its config/docs.
!/.gitignore
!/src/
!/public/
!/migrations/
!/package.json
!/package-lock.json
!/next.config.ts
!/next-env.d.ts
!/tsconfig.json
!/eslint.config.mjs
!/postcss.config.mjs
!/README.md
!/AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md

# guides/ is intentionally NOT tracked: the runbook markdown contains live secrets/creds. The app
# serves it from disk (process.cwd()/guides or AEM_GUIDES_DIR), so it stays untracked on the bastion.

# Belt-and-braces: never track deps, build output, env or secrets even inside tracked dirs.
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.pem
*.log
keys/

# Editor/backup cruft
*.bak*
